(LST2-89 — `treating <match> as <replacement>` substitutes the loop
 variable for that iteration when it equals the match. Works with text
 matches and with number matches, over a list variable, a list literal
 and a range. The manual's own "print with default value" example is the
 first block.
 Also covers: LST2-91 (the print-with-default example), LST2-93 (the
 syntax), LST2-94 (equality with the match drives the substitution).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-89.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   ann
   Anonymous
   bob
   ---
   1
   99
   2
   ---
   1
   2
   300
   4
)
a list called names is ["ann", "", "bob"].
print each name from names treating "" as "Anonymous".
print "---".
a list called codes is [1, 0, 2].
print each code from codes treating 0 as 99.
print "---".
print each step from 1 to 4 treating 3 as 300.
